# Navigation invariants — Hannah's rules

These are hard product rules. Never violate them, no matter how sensible an
edit may look in isolation. If you think one of these needs to change, stop
and ask Hannah before editing the component, the props, the tests, the i18n
keys, or anything else related.

Full explanation and rationale: `docs/design/NAV_INVARIANTS.md`.

## 1. Feedback page placement (MOBILE)

The Feedback page (`/feedback`, "Submit Feedback") MUST NOT appear in the
mobile bottom nav. It lives ONLY in the profile-icon menu in the top-right
corner (`components/layout/MobileAccountPanel.tsx`).

**Forbidden files/locations to add a feedback item to:**
- `components/layout/MobileBottomNav.tsx`
- `components/projects/ProjectMobileBottomNav.tsx`
- Any new file matching `**/*MobileBottomNav*.tsx` or `**/*BottomNav*.tsx`

**Allowed:**
- `components/layout/MobileAccountPanel.tsx` (the profile menu). This is the
  one and only place feedback appears on mobile.

**Enforcement:**
- `__tests__/unit/MobileBottomNav.unit.test.tsx` has an invariant test
  asserting `/feedback` is not in the nav. Do not delete or weaken this
  test. If it starts failing, fix the regressed component.
- `MobileBottomNav.tsx` has a header comment repeating this rule.

**Before editing any bottom-nav component, search for `feedback`, `/feedback`,
and `MessageSquarePlus` / `MessageSquareHeart` icons to confirm you are not
reintroducing the item.**

## Adding new invariants

When Hannah clarifies a nav placement rule a second time, add it to this file
AND to `docs/design/NAV_INVARIANTS.md` in the same commit. Twice-clarified =
belongs in the guardrail.
